后来我和克雷格还有布莱恩一起上了阿尔·罗克主持的《今日秀》。

164
00:07:41.810 --> 00:07:43.690
Al Roker came to Scranton.
阿尔·罗克也去了斯克兰顿。

165
00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:46.810
And we did the Today Show from there with him.
我们就在那儿和他一起录了《今日秀》。

166
00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:50.810
And I mean, it was just a blaSt.
我是说，那真的太好玩了。

167
00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:52.910
I was so jealous.
我当时嫉妒坏了。

168
00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:55.290
That looked like so much fun.
看起来真的很有意思。

169
00:07:55.470 --> 00:07:59.590
You guys did like a whole Q&A panel and like a meet and greet, right?
你们还搞了问答座谈会和粉丝见面会，对吧？

170
00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.090
And we did like a concert.
我们还办了场演唱会。

171
00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:05.490
Like there was a concert and a bunch of people from the office performed like Craig and Melora.
就是有场演唱会，剧组里很多人都上台表演了，比如克雷格和梅洛拉。

172
00:08:05.650 --> 00:08:07.450
Like everyone got up on stage.
大家都上台了。

173
00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:09.250
It was so much fun.
真的特别开心。

174
00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:15.370
But, you know, lady, this was something you and I both share because I was able to go to this convention.
不过，你知道吗，女士，这事儿咱们俩感同身受，因为我能去参加那次大会。

175
00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:20.490
But then at the end of the show, there was another one, like a big wrap party convention.
但后来剧集结束时，又办了一次，像是一场大型的杀青派对大会。

176
00:08:21.050 --> 00:08:22.530
And it was my daughter's birthday.
那天正好是我女儿的生日。

177
00:08:22.530 --> 00:08:23.730
So you went to that one.
所以你去了那一次。

178
00:08:23.850 --> 00:08:30.950
So I found all these emails, Jenna, where we sort of bookend this experience for each other because I went to one and you got to go to the other.
所以我翻到了所有这些邮件，珍娜，我们俩就像是给这段经历画上了圆满的句号，因为我去了其中一个，而你去了另一个。

179
00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:32.890
Yeah, I remember that.
是啊，我记得。

180
00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:43.410
I was so glad I got to go to that one at the end of the show because I couldn't leave the experience of the office having never visited Scranton.
我很高兴我能参加剧集结束时的那次活动，因为我不能在没去过斯克兰顿的情况下就结束《办公室》这段经历。

181
00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:48.230
So I just remember I was really jealous that you got to go and I was bummed that I had to stay home.
所以我只记得当时你去了，我特别嫉妒，而且因为不得不待在家里而感到沮丧。

182
00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:49.430
But, you know.
不过，你知道的。

183
00:08:49.810 --> 00:08:52.790
Well, you know, we've never gotten to go together.
嗯，你知道，我们俩从来没能一起去过。

184
00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:54.590
And that's on my bucket liSt.
那在我的遗愿清单上。

185
00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:59.110
When this podcast is done, I want you and I to go to Scranton.
等这个播客做完，我想和你一起去斯克兰顿。

186
00:08:59.290 --> 00:09:00.730
That's on my wish liSt.
那在我的愿望清单上。

187
00:09:00.730 --> 00:09:06.850
I want you and I to go to Scranton and just anonymously sign up for the office tour.
我想和你一起去斯克兰顿，然后匿名报名参加《办公室》的巡回参观。

188
00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:08.130
Oh, my God.
天哪。

189
00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:11.490
And just show up and be like, take us on the tour.
然后直接出现，说，带我们参观一下吧。

190
00:09:11.730 --> 00:09:13.250
Yes, to all the spots.
没错，去所有那些景点。

191
00:09:13.250 --> 00:09:14.330
I want to do it.
我一定要去。

192
00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.430
Well, listen, there was something else going on during this time.
对了，听着，那段时间还发生了一件事。

193
00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:20.010
I don't know if you remember.
不知道你还记不记得。

194
00:09:20.910 --> 00:09:25.050
But we were on the cover of Entertainment Weekly magazine.
我们登上了《娱乐周刊》的封面。

195
00:09:25.450 --> 00:09:26.290
We were?
我们登上了？

196
00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:30.510
It came out October 5th, which was the day after this episode aired.
那是10月5日发行的，就在这集播出的第二天。

197
00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:33.690
And there were a few sets of couples.
当时有几组情侣封面。

198
00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:37.010
Steve and Melora, as Jan and Michael, were on one cover.
史蒂夫和梅洛拉，作为简和迈克尔，登上了其中一个封面。

199
00:09:37.270 --> 00:09:39.610
And then Angela and Dwight were on one.
然后安吉拉和德怀特登上了另一个。

200
00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:40.930
And Jim and Pam.
还有吉姆和帕姆。

201
00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:43.130
And then Ryan and Kelly.
还有瑞安和凯利。

202
00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:46.010
So you could pick which issue had the cover.
所以你可以选择哪一期作为封面。

203
00:09:46.130 --> 00:09:49.230
But then we were all on the inside in this big group photo.
但我们所有人都出现在内页的那张大合影里。

204
00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:51.410
I remember doing that photo shoot.
我记得拍那张照片的时候。

205
00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:51.910
I know.
我知道。

206
00:09:51.910 --> 00:09:53.090
It was so fun.
真的很有趣。

207
00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.510
It was such a cool day.
那真是很棒的一天。

208
00:09:55.610 --> 00:09:56.410
And I couldn't believe it.
我简直不敢相信。

209
00:09:56.510 --> 00:09:58.850
Like, I'd always, you know, picked up Entertainment Weekly.
就像，你知道，我一直都有买《娱乐周刊》的习惯。

210
00:09:58.850 --> 00:09:59.830
I loved television.
我热爱电视。

211
00:09:59.830 --> 00:10:01.610
It was like my dream to be on TV.
能上电视就像是我的梦想一样。

212
00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:05.630
And then to all of a sudden be on the cover and be in it with you guys.
然后突然之间，我就登上了封面，还和你们大家在一起。

213
00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:07.090
I couldn't even believe it.
我简直无法相信。

214
00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:08.170
I have one framed.
我装裱了一份。

215
00:10:08.770 --> 00:10:13.890
Well, this is what was happening at this time, which was that the show was truly blowing up.
嗯，当时的情况是这样的，这部剧真的火了。

216
00:10:13.890 --> 00:10:17.250
And we were on covers of magazines.
我们登上了各种杂志的封面。

217
00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:19.430
And it was so surreal.
感觉太不真实了。

218
00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:30.270
Early on, I tried to save every single mention of us or the show from any publication because it just felt so fleeting.
起初，我试图保存每一篇提到我们或这部剧的报道，因为我觉得这一切太短暂了。

219
00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:33.530
And then at this time, it became impossible.
但到了这个时候，这已经不可能了。

220
00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:36.090
It was just constant.
简直是源源不断。

221
00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:38.810
And we were really out in the zeitgeiSt.
我们真的成为了时代精神的一部分。

222
00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.370
Is that the right word?
这个词用得对吗？

223
00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.950
Yeah, yeah, no, the show was just really catching on.
对，对，没错，这部剧真的火起来了。

224
00:10:44.210 --> 00:10:51.250
I'll tell you what, between my mom and my grandmother and my cousin Carol and my Aunt Brenda, I think I have everything we were ever mentioned in.
我跟你说，我妈、我奶奶、我表姐卡罗尔还有我布伦达阿姨，我觉得她们把我所有被提及的报道都留下来了。

225
00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:54.490
Because they saved everything and they would send it to me.
因为她们把一切都存了下来，还会寄给我。

226
00:10:54.650 --> 00:11:04.930
Well, speaking of being out in the world in a big way, fast fact number three, we got a lot of fan mail from people about the Dunder Mifflin Infinity website.
说到在世界上产生巨大影响，第三个速览事实，我们收到了很多粉丝关于“邓德·米夫林无限”网站的来信。

227
00:11:06.170 --> 00:11:08.690
And they wanted to know if it was real.
他们想知道那是不是真的。

228
00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.710
Well, it was real.
嗯，那是真的。

229
00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:18.190
And it went out into the world around this exact same time as this episode.
它就在这一集播出的同一时间上线了。

230
00:11:18.370 --> 00:11:19.290
That is right.
没错。

231
00:11:19.310 --> 00:11:21.630
And we reached out to Joya Balfour.
我们联系了乔亚·巴尔福。

232
00:11:21.910 --> 00:11:26.210
Joya, as you remember, Jenna, was part of the team at NBC.com.
乔亚，你还记得吗，珍娜，她是 NBC.com 团队的一员。

233
00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:30.930
And you guys, networks were not doing digital content during this time.
你们知道吗，那时候电视网根本不做数字内容。

234
00:11:31.090 --> 00:11:32.330
It's just something they didn't do.
这在当时是他们根本不会做的事情。

235
00:11:32.530 --> 00:11:34.450
So NBC was really on the forefront.
所以 NBC 真的走在了前沿。

236
00:11:34.450 --> 00:11:42.510
And I talked to Joya, and she was saying they were trying to find ways to sustain the fandom to keep fans engaged.
我和乔亚聊过，她说他们当时在想办法维持粉丝群，让粉丝们保持参与感。

237
00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:46.450
And one of the things they did was they launched Dunder Mifflin Infinity.com.
他们所做的事情之一就是推出了 Dunder Mifflin Infinity.com。

238
00:11:46.590 --> 00:11:48.490
You could go on and play these games.
你可以上去玩这些游戏。

239
00:11:48.690 --> 00:11:51.210
There were virtual branches that fans could join.
网站上有粉丝可以加入的虚拟分部。

240
00:11:51.210 --> 00:11:54.970
They could perform tasks where they would earn Shroot Bucks.
他们可以通过完成任务来赚取“施鲁特币”。

241
00:11:55.150 --> 00:12:00.910
And then they could spend their Shroot Bucks on virtual items in sort of like the office.
然后他们可以用这些“施鲁特币”在办公室里购买虚拟物品。

242
00:12:01.050 --> 00:12:02.970
And they went around to all of our desks.
他们还绕着我们所有的办公桌拍了一圈。

243
00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:07.090
They took pictures of the set so that they could actually buy virtual iteMs.
他们拍下了片场的照片，这样粉丝们就能真正买到虚拟物品了。

244
00:12:07.090 --> 00:12:10.910
And this site ran for three years on NBC.com.
这个网站在 NBC.com 上运行了三年。

245
00:12:11.050 --> 00:12:14.170
And fans got signed items from the show.
粉丝们还能得到剧组的签名物品。

246
00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:19.330
And also, if they submitted their artwork, it would be displayed in episodes.
而且，如果他们提交了自己的艺术作品，还会出现在剧集中。

247
00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:22.890
Jenna, fan art was put around the set.
珍娜，粉丝艺术作品被摆放在了片场各处。

248
00:12:22.890 --> 00:12:24.670
So your art might make it into the show.
所以你的作品可能会出现在剧里。

249
00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:29.090
It might end up on the refrigerator in the kitchen or on a bulletin board like by Creed and Meredith.
它可能会出现在厨房的冰箱上，或者像克里德和梅雷迪思旁边的公告栏上。

250
00:12:29.390 --> 00:12:31.750
And fans could look for their art if they won.
如果粉丝的作品被选中，他们还能在剧里找找看。

251
00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:32.610
Isn't that amazing?
这难道不令人惊叹吗？

252
00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:38.110
It's really incredible because I just want to remind everyone, there was no Instagram.
这真的很不可思议，因为我想提醒大家，那时候还没有 Instagram。

253
00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:40.410
There were no apps back then.
那时候根本没有应用程序。

254
00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:51.590
Like this was really, really revolutionary in terms of that idea of fan engagement and getting to participate in some way actively with your favorite show.
这在粉丝互动以及以某种方式积极参与你最喜爱的节目这一理念上，真的是非常、非常具有革命性的。

255
00:12:51.830 --> 00:12:52.450
Yes.
是的。

256
00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:54.050
And they even made a video.
他们甚至还制作了一个视频。

257
00:12:54.290 --> 00:12:56.770
And actually, I have audio of it.
事实上，我还有它的音频。

258
00:12:56.910 --> 00:13:00.330
Sam, can you play the video of DunderMifflinInfinity.com?
山姆，你能播放一下 DunderMifflinInfinity.com 的视频吗？

