00:15:07.200 --> 00:15:07.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

302
00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:10.880
Because she knows what he likes, because she's his girlfriend.
因为她知道他喜欢什么，因为她是他的女朋友。

303
00:15:11.360 --> 00:15:15.540
And then she gives him a little peck, a little kiss as she's leaving.
然后她离开时给了他轻轻一啄，一个小吻。

304
00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:17.120
But Toby sees.
但托比看到了。

305
00:15:17.660 --> 00:15:19.780
Can we talk about Paul's expression?
我们能聊聊保罗的表情吗？

306
00:15:20.760 --> 00:15:21.540
We can.
可以。

307
00:15:21.540 --> 00:15:23.800
I froze on his face.
我把画面定格在他的脸上。

308
00:15:23.980 --> 00:15:25.260
I was laughing so hard.
我当时笑得不行。

309
00:15:25.360 --> 00:15:27.460
I don't even know what all it's conveying.
我甚至不知道那表情传达了什么。

310
00:15:27.600 --> 00:15:30.820
It's conveying so many things at 20 seconds, Toby's face.
在20秒的时候，托比的表情传达了太多东西。

311
00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:35.380
Well, Paul does some amazing reaction acting in this episode.
嗯，保罗在这一集里贡献了非常精彩的反应戏。

312
00:15:35.380 --> 00:15:42.760
If you are an actor and you would like to study great reactions, this is a real good one to study.
如果你是一名演员，想学习如何做出精彩的反应，这一段非常值得研究。

313
00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:43.240
Yeah.
没错。

314
00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:53.320
Well, what happens after this is that Toby puts out a memo regarding PDA in the workplace, and everyone's reading it.
嗯，接下来发生的事是，托比发了一份关于职场公开亲热的备忘录，大家都在看。

315
00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:56.060
And Jim and Pam are like, what is this about?
吉姆和帕姆心想，这是什么意思？

316
00:15:56.420 --> 00:15:58.240
Toby is so passive aggressive.
托比真是太消极怠工了。

317
00:15:58.620 --> 00:15:59.500
He really is.
确实如此。

318
00:15:59.640 --> 00:16:02.840
He clearly has issue, but he's going to put out a memo?
他明明有意见，却要发个备忘录？

319
00:16:03.080 --> 00:16:03.800
Come on, Toby.
拜托，托比。

320
00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:10.600
Well, Michael thinks that the memo is about that night that he and Jan did some stuff in his office.
嗯，迈克尔以为备忘录是针对他和简在他办公室里做的那点事。

321
00:16:10.600 --> 00:16:14.180
But, I mean, he says almost everyone was gone for the day.
但我的意思是，他说当时几乎所有人都下班了。

322
00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.940
This is ridiculous, Toby.
这太荒谬了，托比。

323
00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:17.920
Yeah.
是啊。

324
00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:28.460
And then Angela thinks it might be about her and Dwight, so she yells from across the room and makes this big statement that she's never been intimate with anyone in the office.
然后安吉拉以为是在说她和德怀特，所以她隔着房间大喊，郑重声明她从未和办公室里的任何人有过亲密关系。

325
00:16:28.460 --> 00:16:36.000
And that is when Toby says, no, no, it was a complaint about Jim and Pam.
就在那时，托比说，不，不，这是关于吉姆和帕姆的投诉。

326
00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:40.500
And then he basically outs their relationship to the whole office.
然后他基本上向整个办公室公开了他们的恋情。

327
00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:45.680
I mean, Toby, this is twice now because he did this with Oscar.
我是说，托比，这已经是第二次了，因为他之前对奥斯卡也干过这种事。

328
00:16:46.140 --> 00:16:53.680
And now with Jim and Pam, he's announced that they're dating and everyone freaks out, but no one freaks out more than Michael.
现在轮到吉姆和帕姆了，他宣布他们在约会，大家都惊呆了，但最震惊的莫过于迈克尔。

329
00:16:53.900 --> 00:16:55.960
Well, Michael is giddy.
嗯，迈克尔乐坏了。

330
00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:58.040
Michael doesn't even know what to do with himself.
迈克尔甚至不知道该怎么办才好。

331
00:16:58.040 --> 00:17:01.560
And Steve's performance is so sweet.
史蒂夫的表演太可爱了。

332
00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:06.160
He is so genuinely excited that Jim and Pam are together.
他是真心为吉姆和帕姆在一起感到高兴。

333
00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:10.560
He makes them hold hands and he makes a big declaration.
他强迫他们牵手，还发表了一番宏大的宣言。

334
00:17:11.040 --> 00:17:13.560
This day will go down in infamy.
这一天将作为耻辱日载入史册。

335
00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:18.460
He makes you guys hold hands and then he really bear hugs Jim.
他让你们牵手，然后给了吉姆一个大大的熊抱。

336
00:17:18.660 --> 00:17:21.140
And then he goes to hug you, but your phone starts ringing.
接着他想去抱你，但你的电话响了。

337
00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:24.460
And Pam's like, oh, like rescued by my phone.
帕姆当时想，哦，电话救了我一命。

338
00:17:24.460 --> 00:17:28.120
And he's like, no, no, Pam, let it ring.
他说，不，不，帕姆，让它响吧。

339
00:17:28.300 --> 00:17:31.160
Let the bells of Dunder Mifflin chime out your love.
让邓德·米夫林的钟声为你俩的爱情鸣响吧。

340
00:17:32.640 --> 00:17:39.460
But then he has that really famous line that I've seen people write on their graduation hats.
然后他说了那句非常有名的台词，我见过有人把它写在毕业帽上。

341
00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:40.640
I've seen it everywhere.
我到处都见过。

342
00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:44.780
I've seen it like stitched on a pillow, on a graduation hat.
我见过把它绣在枕头上，写在毕业帽上。

343
00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:46.220
It's so good.
太棒了。

344
00:17:46.400 --> 00:17:47.200
Say it, Ange.
说出来吧，安吉。

345
00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.940
My heart soars with the eagle's neSt.
我的心随着鹰巢高高飞翔。

346
00:17:50.280 --> 00:17:50.720
Incredible.
不可思议。

347
00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:55.320
Now we said this episode was written by Mike Schur, and that has to be a Mike Schur special right there.
我们说过这一集是迈克·舒尔写的，那一定是迈克·舒尔的招牌台词。

348
00:17:55.480 --> 00:17:56.540
It has to be.
一定是。

349
00:17:56.700 --> 00:17:58.860
Now we see a series of talking heads.
现在我们看到了一系列采访镜头。

350
00:17:59.060 --> 00:18:03.300
And Jenna, I was very curious about this because you like to deep dive on positioning.
珍娜，我对这个很好奇，因为你喜欢深入研究站位。

351
00:18:04.440 --> 00:18:06.240
Oh, that sounds like that's what she said.
哦，听起来像是她说的那样。

352
00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:10.540
It sounded different than what I think you mean, but go on.
听起来跟我以为的意思不太一样，但你继续。

353
00:18:13.240 --> 00:18:15.900
As it was coming out of my mouth, I knew it was wrong.
话刚出口我就知道说错了。

354
00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:17.400
Ah, that's what she said.
啊，那就是她说的那样。

355
00:18:17.480 --> 00:18:18.760
That's what she said.
那就是她说的那样。

356
00:18:18.960 --> 00:18:20.180
So Dwight's talking head.
所以是德怀特的个人采访。

357
00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.360
He's like, I don't see it.
他说，我不觉得。

358
00:18:21.460 --> 00:18:22.620
I think they could do better.
我觉得他们可以做得更好。

359
00:18:22.880 --> 00:18:29.340
He is sitting in front of the wall, and off of his left shoulder is the bullpen, right?
他坐在墙前面，左肩外侧是办公区，对吧？

360
00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:29.640
Yep.
没错。

361
00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.100
Yep.
没错。

362
00:18:30.540 --> 00:18:35.720
Then it cuts to me, and I say, I'm not surprised, Pam is the office mattress.
然后切到我，我说，我不惊讶，帕姆是办公室里的公共汽车。

363
00:18:36.240 --> 00:18:37.600
Which is such a great line.
那真是一句绝妙的台词。

364
00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:43.220
But I'm sitting in front of the window with the wall to my right shoulder.
但我坐在窗户前面，右肩对着墙。

365
00:18:44.000 --> 00:18:49.600
Yeah, there's more wall and more window, depending on who's talking head it is.
是啊，根据是谁的个人采访，墙和窗户的比例也不一样。

366
00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:51.880
It's not always the exact same shot.
镜头并不总是完全一样的。

367
00:18:52.060 --> 00:18:52.780
I noticed that, too.
我也注意到了。

368
00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:58.320
And then it cuts to Andy, and he's framed the exact same way that Dwight was.
然后切到安迪，他的构图和德怀特完全一样。

369
00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:04.620
And I realize I'm becoming one of the fans of the show where I'm like, is there something there?
我意识到自己正变成那种会想“这里面是不是有什么名堂”的剧迷。

370
00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:09.540
But I'm like, this is an interesting love triangle that's about to play out.
但我心想，这即将上演一段有趣的三角恋。

371
00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.340
And this is a little bit of a Dwight-Angela-Andy sandwich.
这简直就是德怀特、安吉拉和安迪的三明治夹心。

372
00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:15.500
I don't think you are reading into it.
我觉得你没想多。

373
00:19:15.580 --> 00:19:16.760
I noticed the same thing.
我也注意到了同样的事。

374
00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:23.900
I feel like they purposely didn't set all the shots the same, and they also differentiated Angela from the two men.
我觉得他们是有意不把所有镜头拍得一样，而且他们还把安吉拉和那两个男人区分开了。

375
00:19:24.320 --> 00:19:24.640
Yeah.
是啊。

376
00:19:24.920 --> 00:19:26.100
That can't be an accident.
那不可能是巧合。

377
00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:27.180
It can't be.
不可能。

378
00:19:27.180 --> 00:19:28.180
All right.
好吧。

379
00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:30.400
Well, now we're going to get into the episode, right?
那么，现在我们要进入这一集了，对吧？

380
00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:34.480
We have our opening credits, and the first scene is the party planning committee.
片头过后，第一个场景是派对策划委员会。

381
00:19:34.720 --> 00:19:36.660
They're setting up for Ryan's return.
她们正在为瑞安的回归做准备。

382
00:19:37.180 --> 00:19:40.640
Phyllis and Angela are hanging a banner that says, Welcome Back, Ryan.
菲利斯和安吉拉正在挂一条写着“欢迎回来，瑞安”的横幅。

383
00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:42.940
Three minutes, 28 seconds.
三分二十八秒。

384
00:19:43.300 --> 00:19:44.020
Skin alert.
露肤警报。

385
00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:45.220
What's a skin alert?
什么是露肤警报？

386
00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:50.180
Well, my sweater in this episode, I feel like the dry-clean shrunk it.
嗯，这一集里我穿的毛衣，我觉得干洗店把它洗缩水了。

387
00:19:50.280 --> 00:19:53.040
Like, it fit one day, and then the next day it got a little tighter.
就像有一天还合身，第二天就变紧了。

388
00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:56.440
And as I'm hanging the banner, you see, like, my midriff.
当我挂横幅的时候，你能看到我的腰部。

389
00:19:57.120 --> 00:19:58.280
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

390
00:19:58.280 --> 00:20:00.200
That's very out of character for Angela Martin.
这太不符合安吉拉·马丁的性格了。

391
00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:00.780
It's very scandalous.
这太伤风败俗了。

392
00:20:00.920 --> 00:20:01.560
It's scandalous.
太伤风败俗了。

393
00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:04.560
Well, double skin alert, Kelly arrives.
好吧，双重露肤警报，凯莉到了。

394
00:20:04.840 --> 00:20:05.180
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

395
00:20:05.500 --> 00:20:07.220
She is all zhuzhed up.
她打扮得花枝招展的。

396
00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:10.100
She's like, Oh, is Ryan coming back today?
她说，哦，瑞安今天要回来吗？

397
00:20:10.100 --> 00:20:11.560
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

398
00:20:12.040 --> 00:20:13.700
She looks super cutie pie.
她看起来超级可爱。

399
00:20:13.920 --> 00:20:15.400
She looks super cutie pie.
她看起来超级可爱。

400
00:20:15.720 --> 00:20:20.780
We also, in this scene, have a list of that's what she said that Michael had ready to go.
在这一幕里，我们还有一份迈克尔准备好的“她说的那样”的清单。

401
00:20:21.480 --> 00:20:23.280
Oh, please, please read it.
噢，拜托，拜托读一下。

402
00:20:23.540 --> 00:20:24.100
Here it is.
在这儿。

403
00:20:24.500 --> 00:20:25.860
Can you make that straighter?
你能把它弄直一点吗？

404
00:20:26.520 --> 00:20:27.700
That job looks hard.
那活儿看起来挺难的。

405
00:20:28.020 --> 00:20:29.540
You should put your mouth on that.
你应该把嘴凑上去。

406
00:20:29.900 --> 00:20:31.700
You might want to trim it a little.
你可能得稍微修剪一下。

407
00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:33.640
Yeah.
是啊。

408
00:20:33.980 --> 00:20:34.260
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

409
00:20:34.640 --> 00:20:35.200
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

410
00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:38.920
I liked it when he said, You might want to put your mouth on that.
他说“你可能得把嘴凑上去”的时候，我挺喜欢的。

411
00:20:39.060 --> 00:20:41.080
And Pam says, How?
然后帕姆说，怎么凑？

412
00:20:41.220 --> 00:20:44.600
I don't understand how you were even planning to use that naturally.
我真不明白你当时是怎么打算自然地用上那句话的。

413
00:20:45.040 --> 00:20:45.220
Yeah.
是啊。

414
00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:49.240
And he was like, under his breath, he's like, If you were blowing up balloons.
然后他小声嘟囔了一句，他说，如果你是在吹气球的话。

415
00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.020
I was just, I don't know.
我当时就是，我不知道。

416
00:20:51.240 --> 00:20:51.580
Just balloons.
就是气球而已。

417
00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:52.500
I had it ready.
我当时准备好了。

418
00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:53.700
I was ready to go.
我准备好开始了。

419
00:20:53.880 --> 00:20:57.660
Well, now we have sort of an interesting little spy shot.
好吧，现在我们有了一个挺有意思的偷拍镜头。

420
00:20:57.880 --> 00:21:06.320
We've got some black and white footage of the elevator bay, which is meant to be, I guess, security camera footage.
我们有一些电梯厅的黑白录像，我想那应该是安保监控录像。

421
00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.320
Yeah, but this is like something we don't do on the show.
是啊，但这在我们剧里是不常有的。

422
00:21:09.320 --> 00:21:13.760
So it was jarring to me when I saw it again because I hadn't seen this episode in so long.
所以我再看到的时候觉得很突兀，因为我好久没看这一集了。

423
00:21:13.900 --> 00:21:16.480
And I was like, Whoa, what's up with the security camera footage?
当时我就想，哇，这安保监控录像是什么情况？

424
00:21:16.480 --> 00:21:23.880
Well, what was odd is that we then switch to a spy shot from our regular documentary camera.
嗯，奇怪的是，我们随后切换到了常规纪录片摄像机的偷拍视角。

425
00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:24.440
Yeah.
是啊。

426
00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:28.340
So it was a little bit, I found it a little bit odd as well.
所以我当时也觉得有点奇怪。

427
00:21:28.440 --> 00:21:30.860
But that's what that black and white footage is supposed to be.
但那段黑白录像本意就是那样。

428
00:21:31.020 --> 00:21:42.780
And the reason they're showing this is because Dwight and Angela have met in this elevator vestibule so that he can present her with a new cat, a feral barn cat.
之所以展示这个，是因为德怀特和安吉拉在电梯厅见面，他要送她一只新猫，一只野生的谷仓猫。

429
00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:43.460
Feral?
野生的（Feral）？

430
00:21:44.380 --> 00:21:45.020
Feral?
野生的（Feral）？

431
00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:45.560
Feral?
野生的（Feral）？

432
00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:47.160
How do you say feral?
你怎么读“野生的”这个词？

433
00:21:47.640 --> 00:21:48.240
Feral?
野生的（Feral）？

434
00:21:48.480 --> 00:21:48.660
Feral?
野生的（Feral）？

435
00:21:48.860 --> 00:21:49.720
Tomato, tomato?
就像番茄（Tomato）和番茄（Tomato）的读法不同一样？

436
00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:50.920
You say feral?
你读作“Feral”？

437
00:21:51.380 --> 00:21:51.920
Feral.
Feral。

438
00:21:52.540 --> 00:21:54.240
A feral cat?
一只野猫？

439
00:21:54.580 --> 00:21:55.860
A feral cat.
一只野猫。

440
00:21:56.080 --> 00:21:56.440
Feral?
Feral？

441
00:21:56.680 --> 00:21:56.920
Feral.
Feral。

442
00:21:57.220 --> 00:21:58.620
It's feral, right?
是读Feral，对吧？

443
00:21:58.800 --> 00:21:59.900
It's tomato, tomato.
这就是番茄和番茄的区别。

444
00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:00.600
Sam?
萨姆？

445
00:22:00.860 --> 00:22:01.160
Feral.
Feral。

446
00:22:02.200 --> 00:22:03.980
Sam sided with me!
萨姆站在我这边！

447
00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:06.220
And Dwight says feral in the episode.
而且德怀特在剧里也是读的Feral。

448
00:22:06.220 --> 00:22:12.720
But anyway, Jenna, we'll just chunk that aside and let you say feral.
不过总之，珍娜，我们先把这个放一边，让你读Feral吧。

449
00:22:15.740 --> 00:22:18.220
Listeners, do any of you say feral?
听众朋友们，你们有人读Feral吗？

450
00:22:18.380 --> 00:22:18.900
Please write us.
请写信告诉我们。

451
00:22:20.620 --> 00:22:21.260
All right.
好吧。

452
00:22:21.480 --> 00:22:23.380
So, yes, Dwight gives her garbage.
所以，没错，德怀特给了她垃圾。

453
00:22:23.900 --> 00:22:30.620
And this poor cat, they put, like, stuff in its hair to make it look kind of grungy, like it had been eating garbage.
这只可怜的猫，他们往它毛里弄了些东西，让它看起来脏兮兮的，就像是吃垃圾长大的一样。

454
00:22:30.620 --> 00:22:33.660
Well, we had a fan question from Rivka Wasserman.
我们收到了一位粉丝里夫卡·瓦瑟曼的提问。

455
00:22:33.920 --> 00:22:38.520
Did they gel the cat's hair before the shoot to make him look like more of a stray cat?
他们在拍摄前给猫的毛抹了发胶，好让它看起来更像流浪猫吗？

456
00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:46.920
Well, I reached out to Kim Ferry and she said they did, that her memory is that the trainer had a little bit of honey.
我联系了金·费里，她说确实抹了，她记得驯兽师用了一点蜂蜜。

457
00:22:47.620 --> 00:22:55.640
We had warned the trainer of this very well-trained, domesticated cat that we wanted it to look feral.
我们曾叮嘱过这只训练有素的家猫的驯兽师，我们希望它看起来野性一点。

458
00:22:56.160 --> 00:23:02.800
And so they suggested something natural like honey to kind of rough up the cat's fur.
所以他们建议用蜂蜜这种天然的东西来弄乱猫的毛。

459
00:23:02.980 --> 00:23:04.420
And so that's what they used.
于是他们就用了这个。

460
00:23:04.800 --> 00:23:07.260
Yes, these trainers were so great with the cats.
没错，这些驯兽师对猫真的太棒了。

461
00:23:07.420 --> 00:23:12.020
And obviously, honey isn't going to do anything, you know, that's just, like, organic.
显然，蜂蜜不会有什么影响，你知道的，那只是有机的。

462
00:23:12.360 --> 00:23:14.940
I do have amazing memories of this scene.
我对这场戏的记忆非常深刻。

463
00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:20.780
I want you guys to know that this cat was crawling all over Rain, all over him.
我想让你们知道，这只猫在雷恩身上爬来爬去，到处都是。

464
00:23:21.280 --> 00:23:23.580
Well, you can see it in the episode.
你们在剧集里也能看出来。

465
00:23:23.780 --> 00:23:26.420
Like, every shot, the cat is in a different position.
你看，每一个镜头里，猫的位置都不一样。

466
00:23:26.480 --> 00:23:28.820
It kept jumping out of his arMs.
它一直从他怀里跳出来。

467
00:23:29.020 --> 00:23:40.360
And so we really had to sort of deliver the emotion of the scene but get our lines out quickly because this thing was climbing off Rain and wanted to go exploring the whole scene.
所以我们真的必须一边传达出戏里的情绪，一边快速说出台词，因为这小家伙一直在往雷恩身上爬，还想去探索整个片场。

468
00:23:42.180 --> 00:23:47.420
Well, my favorite is the shot where it's, like, clearly crawling over his shoulder.
我最喜欢的一个镜头是它明显爬在他肩膀上的那个。

469
00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:50.340
And then one second later, he's holding it like a baby.
然后一秒钟后，他又像抱婴儿一样抱着它。

470
00:23:50.700 --> 00:23:51.060
Yeah.
是啊。

471
00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:52.300
In his arMs.
在他怀里。

472
00:23:52.480 --> 00:23:53.100
Because it's amazing.
因为它太神奇了。

473
00:23:53.300 --> 00:23:54.500
Clearly, the cat was everywhere.
很明显，这只猫到处乱跑。

474
00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:55.480
The cat was everywhere.
猫到处都是。

475
00:23:55.500 --> 00:23:59.960
And the cat wranglers were, like, stepping in and being like, okay, here, try holding him this way.
驯猫师不得不介入，说，好的，来，试着这样抱它。

476
00:24:00.240 --> 00:24:00.760
Try this.
试试这个。

477
00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:08.240
When the cat jumps out of Rain's arms at the end, that was, like, the easiest moment to film because it wanted to go explore.
最后猫从雷恩怀里跳出来的时候，那是拍摄起来最轻松的时刻，因为它想去探索。

478
00:24:09.140 --> 00:24:16.060
Well, Ange, a lot of people asked if this was the same cat that Andy gives you later that becomes Bandit.
安吉，很多人问这只猫是不是后来安迪送给你的那只，也就是后来的“强盗”。

479
00:24:16.700 --> 00:24:21.380
I mean, it's – I wouldn't think it was meant to be the same cat.
我是说，我觉得它本意应该不是同一只猫。

480
00:24:21.500 --> 00:24:29.960
Like, I think what they're thinking is, oh, Dwight lets this cat go, and then years later, Andy finds it again and calls it Bandit.
我觉得大家的想法是，哦，德怀特放走了这只猫，几年后，安迪又发现了它，并叫它“强盗”。

481
00:24:30.100 --> 00:24:31.440
Well, that would be hilarious.
那确实会很搞笑。

482
00:24:31.440 --> 00:24:33.720
But that was never conveyed to us in the script.
但剧本里从来没传达过这个意思。

483
00:24:33.720 --> 00:24:36.740
It's just that Andy wants to give Angela a cat.
只是安迪想送安吉拉一只猫而已。

484
00:24:36.740 --> 00:24:44.180
What I found interesting about that, and obviously we're going to get to that episode, is that Angela accepts the cat from Andy, right?
关于这一点我觉得很有趣的是，显然我们之后会讲到那一集，安吉拉接受了安迪送的猫，对吧？

485
00:24:44.340 --> 00:24:44.500
Yeah.
没错。

486
00:24:44.640 --> 00:24:46.500
But does not accept the cat from Dwight.
但她没有接受德怀特送的猫。

487
00:24:46.620 --> 00:24:53.860
And does it right in front of Dwight to sort of, you know, just really drive the point home that he's not her fella anymore.
而且她当着德怀特的面这么做，就是为了强调他已经不再是她的男人了。

488
00:24:53.860 --> 00:24:58.100
Well, as a person who worked in animal rescue for years and years,
作为一个在动物救援中心工作多年的人，

489
00:24:58.300 --> 00:25:14.140
I will tell you that I don't recommend giving pets as gifts because so many of the pets that are surrendered were gifts that people were not prepared to take care of in the long run or they break up or whatever happens.
我得说我不建议把宠物当作礼物送人，因为很多被遗弃的宠物都是因为人们没有做好长期照顾的准备，或者因为分手之类的原因而被送走的。

490
00:25:14.780 --> 00:25:20.800
I just think people should pick their own pets, or really what my mom always said is, let the pet pick you.
我觉得人们应该自己挑选宠物，或者像我妈妈常说的那样，让宠物来挑选你。

491
00:25:22.100 --> 00:25:23.680
That's how you get your match.
那样你才能找到最适合你的。

492
00:25:24.020 --> 00:25:24.240
Yeah.
是啊。

493
00:25:24.680 --> 00:25:25.800
I like that.
我喜欢这个说法。

494
00:25:26.180 --> 00:25:28.800
I definitely feel our pets picked us for sure.
我绝对觉得我们的宠物肯定是挑选了我们。

495
00:25:29.120 --> 00:25:30.580
Yeah, that's how we got sunny.
没错，我们就是这样得到桑尼的。

496
00:25:30.800 --> 00:25:39.380
We went into this rescue center because we were told that one of the volunteers was going to bring in this box of fluffy gray and white cats.
我们去了那家救援中心，因为有人告诉我们，其中一位志愿者会带一箱毛茸茸的灰白小猫过来。

497
00:25:39.380 --> 00:25:40.500
They were so cute.
它们太可爱了。

498
00:25:40.640 --> 00:25:41.800
They'd sent us pictures.
他们还发了照片给我们。

499
00:25:42.020 --> 00:25:43.440
My daughter was all excited.
我女儿兴奋极了。

500
00:25:43.900 --> 00:25:46.280
And we got there and the woman was running late.
我们到了那里，但那位女士迟到了。

501
00:25:46.280 --> 00:25:51.240
So they took us into a room with all of these adoptable cats and kittens.
他们把我们带进了一个房间，里面全是等待领养的猫咪和幼猫。

502
00:25:51.500 --> 00:25:55.380
And this one little scrappy orange fella would not leave us alone.
有一只瘦小又顽皮的橘猫一直缠着我们不放。

503
00:25:56.040 --> 00:26:00.340
I always say it was like he walked up to us and he was like, hey, guys, what's up?
我总说，当时他就像是走到我们面前，然后说，嘿，伙计们，怎么了？

504
00:26:00.420 --> 00:26:00.880
Good to see you.
见到你们真高兴。

505
00:26:00.920 --> 00:26:01.480
My name's Sunny.
我叫桑尼。

506
00:26:01.480 --> 00:26:02.680
I'll be coming home with you.
我要跟你们回家了。

507
00:26:02.840 --> 00:26:07.840
You can take a look at these other guys if you want, but I will be your cat.
你们想看其他猫也行，但我注定是你们的猫。

508
00:26:07.840 --> 00:26:09.940
But yeah, and that's kind of how we got Sunny.
总之，我们就是这样领养了桑尼。

509
00:26:10.060 --> 00:26:11.000
He wouldn't leave us alone.
他就是不肯离开我们。

510
00:26:11.200 --> 00:26:12.480
Yeah, we could never been happier.
是啊，我们再幸福不过了。

511
00:26:12.720 --> 00:26:13.680
That was Biscuit.
那是饼干。

512
00:26:13.780 --> 00:26:15.440
Biscuit just tried to hide in my sweatshirt.
饼干刚才试图钻进我的运动衫里。

513
00:26:15.580 --> 00:26:17.260
And I thought, well, you got to come home with me now.
我就想，好吧，你现在必须跟我回家了。

514
00:26:17.840 --> 00:26:18.240
Exactly.
没错。

515
00:26:18.620 --> 00:26:19.580
My sweatshirt is your home.
我的运动衫就是你的家。

516
00:26:20.220 --> 00:26:23.000
Well, listen, switching gears back to the show.
好了，听着，我们把话题转回节目吧。

517
00:26:23.300 --> 00:26:25.980
Yeah, don't get us started on our rescue pets.
是啊，别让我们聊起自己的救援宠物。

518
00:26:26.180 --> 00:26:27.940
It'd be a huge tangent.
那话题可就扯远了。

519
00:26:28.820 --> 00:26:35.400
Pam and Jim are going to go to Toby and offer to sign one of the famous love documents.
帕姆和吉姆去找托比，提出要签署那份著名的爱情协议。

520
00:26:35.920 --> 00:26:38.620
Yes, the relationship disclosure form.
没错，就是那份恋爱关系披露表。

521
00:26:38.920 --> 00:26:40.360
And Toby's like, you know what?
然后托比就说，你们知道吗？

522
00:26:41.320 --> 00:26:42.920
That's only for people who are serious.
那只有认真交往的人才能签。

523
00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:45.280
And he's sort of implying this isn't serious, right?
他是在暗示这段关系不认真，对吧？

524
00:26:45.380 --> 00:26:47.460
Because, you know, Toby has his big crush on Pam.
因为，你知道的，托比一直暗恋着帕姆。

525
00:26:47.700 --> 00:26:49.620
And so he's hoping this is casual.
所以他希望这只是随便玩玩。

526
00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:56.080
But Jenna, there's a great scene in the bloopers where at the end of the scene, Toby just tries
但是珍娜，花絮里有一段很棒的戏，在场景结束时，托比试图

527
00:26:56.080 --> 00:26:58.640
to hold Pam's hand in front of Jim.
在吉姆面前牵帕姆的手。

528
00:26:59.120 --> 00:27:00.680
And you guys couldn't get through it.
你们当时根本演不下去。

529
00:27:00.760 --> 00:27:01.480
You just start laughing.
你们直接笑场了。

530
00:27:01.900 --> 00:27:03.480
I remember trying to shoot that.
我记得当时在拍那场戏。

531
00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:04.780
But I don't think we ever got it.
但我认为我们最终没能拍成。

532
00:27:04.880 --> 00:27:06.480
And that's why we never included it.
所以我们才没把它放进正片里。

533
00:27:06.560 --> 00:27:09.840
But it was also just something we thought was so funny in the moment.
但当时我们觉得那一幕真的太搞笑了。

534
00:27:10.160 --> 00:27:16.360
It was like an improvisation that Toby would slowly try to hold Pam's hand during the scene
那就像是即兴表演，托比在戏里慢慢地试图去牵帕姆的手，

535
00:27:16.360 --> 00:27:18.500
and squeeze her hand.
还捏了捏她的手。

536
00:27:18.760 --> 00:27:18.860
Yeah.
没错。

537
00:27:19.020 --> 00:27:20.540
And Jim's like, what's happening?
而吉姆的反应是，这到底在干嘛？

538
00:27:23.630 --> 00:27:26.530
Well, then Ryan returns.
好吧，接着瑞安回归了。

539
00:27:27.410 --> 00:27:33.130
Yes, Ryan, with his new look and his love of blackberries, walks in.
是的，瑞安带着他的新造型和他对黑莓手机的热爱走了进来。

540
00:27:33.610 --> 00:27:34.470
Oh, my God.
天哪。

541
00:27:35.410 --> 00:27:37.950
BJ's performance is so good.
BJ的表演太棒了。

542
00:27:38.010 --> 00:27:41.830
When he's absorbed in his phone and Pam's like, hey, Ryan.
当他沉迷于手机时，帕姆说，嘿，瑞安。

543
00:27:41.950 --> 00:27:42.870
Well, he's like, one second.
他却说，等一下。

544
00:27:44.230 --> 00:27:49.430
And then, like, after he's done typing, he puts it down and he's like, hey, Pam, how's
然后，等他打完字，放下手机说，嘿，帕姆，最近

545
00:27:49.430 --> 00:27:49.790
it going?
怎么样？

546
00:27:49.810 --> 00:27:50.850
It was so good.
演得太好了。

547
00:27:50.850 --> 00:27:55.030
Well, you know, in this scene, I know what you guys are all really here to find out about
好吧，你知道，在这场戏里，我知道你们大家真正想了解的是

548
00:27:55.030 --> 00:27:57.150
is a sad plant alert.
悲伤植物警报。

549
00:27:57.890 --> 00:27:58.670
Oh, no.
噢，不。

550
00:27:59.750 --> 00:28:02.190
Six minutes, seven seconds, sad plant.
六分零七秒，悲伤植物。

551
00:28:02.410 --> 00:28:06.130
I think Pam now for sure the plants aren't going to have a chance because she's in love.
我觉得帕姆现在肯定没心思管那些植物了，因为她坠入爱河了。

552
00:28:07.070 --> 00:28:09.130
Yeah, she doesn't have time for that.
是啊，她没时间管那些。

553
00:28:09.270 --> 00:28:13.930
It's the tiniest little, like, two, like, green leaves sticking out of the pot.
那盆里就冒出两片极小的绿叶，就像那样。

554
00:28:14.050 --> 00:28:14.890
It's like so tiny.
真的太小了。

555
00:28:14.890 --> 00:28:20.270
Well, the thing that I remember about this scene, Angela, is when the character of Kevin
安吉拉，关于这场戏我记得的是，当凯文这个角色

556
00:28:20.270 --> 00:28:24.150
runs up to Ryan and, like, ruffles his hair.
跑向瑞安，揉乱他的头发时。

557
00:28:24.290 --> 00:28:25.170
He gives him a noogie.
他给了他一个脑瓜崩。

558
00:28:25.490 --> 00:28:27.510
He, like, puts him in a headlock and gives him a noogie.
他像这样锁住他的头，给了他一个脑瓜崩。

559
00:28:27.730 --> 00:28:29.730
Those guys could not get through that moment.
那几个家伙当时怎么也演不下去。

560
00:28:30.690 --> 00:28:33.270
Every time it would make BJ laugh.
每次都会把BJ逗笑。

561
00:28:33.430 --> 00:28:35.990
BJ thought it was so funny and he would break.
BJ觉得太搞笑了，他总是会笑场。

562
00:28:35.990 --> 00:28:38.250
And I remember we couldn't get through it.
我记得我们当时怎么也拍不完。

563
00:28:38.350 --> 00:28:39.550
And Brian, too.
布莱恩也是。

564
00:28:39.830 --> 00:28:42.270
I loved it when he's like, fire guy.
我特别喜欢他说“火男”的时候。

565
00:28:42.270 --> 00:28:44.090
And then Andy comes over and he's like, fire guy.
然后安迪走过来，也说“火男”。

566
00:28:44.390 --> 00:28:45.210
And Brian is Kevin.
布莱恩演的是凯文。

567
00:28:45.330 --> 00:28:46.470
He's like, you weren't here for that.
他说，你当时又不在场。

568
00:28:47.350 --> 00:28:48.170
I know.
我知道。

569
00:28:48.570 --> 00:28:50.870
And then Andy says, here for what?
然后安迪说，在场什么？

570
00:28:51.250 --> 00:28:51.490
Yeah.
是啊。

571
00:28:52.430 --> 00:28:53.130
It's so good.
太棒了。

572
00:28:53.270 --> 00:28:54.110
It's so good.
太棒了。

573
00:28:54.310 --> 00:28:57.130
Well, we had a fan question from Lauren C.
我们收到一个来自劳伦·C的粉丝提问。

574
00:28:58.010 --> 00:29:01.310
She wanted to know about Ryan's new look.
她想了解瑞安的新造型。

575
00:29:01.470 --> 00:29:04.010
You know, he's got the facial stubble.
你看，他留了胡茬。

576
00:29:04.270 --> 00:29:05.750
He's slicked his hair back.
头发向后梳得油亮。

577
00:29:05.890 --> 00:29:07.290
He's wearing a fancy suit.
穿着一身考究的西装。

578
00:29:07.290 --> 00:29:12.570
Lauren wants to know, was BJ told to grow facial hair for this season where he's the boss?
劳伦想知道，BJ在这一季当上老板时，是被要求留胡子的吗？

579
00:29:12.590 --> 00:29:15.010
Or did he just personally decide to grow some?
还是他自己决定留的？

580
00:29:15.190 --> 00:29:17.130
Well, I texted BJ about this.
我为此给BJ发了短信。

581
00:29:17.310 --> 00:29:21.070
He said this look was definitely not a personal choice.
他说这个造型绝对不是他个人的选择。

582
00:29:22.850 --> 00:29:25.930
He said he thinks it was a pitch by Jean and Lee.
他说他觉得这是吉恩和李的主意。

583
00:29:26.410 --> 00:29:28.850
At first, the pitch was a goatee.
起初，他们提议留山羊胡。

584
00:29:29.450 --> 00:29:30.970
But Greg said no.
但格雷格拒绝了。

585
00:29:31.190 --> 00:29:32.790
He said it was too on the nose.
他说那样太刻意了。

586
00:29:32.790 --> 00:29:34.710
Yeah, go-to is too much.
没错，山羊胡太夸张了。

587
00:29:34.870 --> 00:29:39.150
The whole look was very kind of like Gordon Gekko, you know, the movie Wall Street.
整个造型有点像戈登·盖柯，就是电影《华尔街》里的那个角色。

588
00:29:39.430 --> 00:29:42.410
It was like, you know, Ryan thinks he's the king of New York now.
就像是，你知道，瑞安觉得自己现在是纽约之王了。

589
00:29:43.270 --> 00:29:43.610
Yes.
没错。

590
00:29:44.290 --> 00:29:48.830
BJ said that he always just kind of rolled with pitches like this.
BJ说他总是顺应这类提议。

591
00:29:48.990 --> 00:29:52.090
And then he said, case in point, the upcoming blonde hair.
然后他说，举个例子，接下来他还要染金发。

592
00:29:52.630 --> 00:29:53.130
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

593
00:29:53.490 --> 00:29:53.850
Yeah.
是啊。

594
00:29:55.570 --> 00:29:58.510
Ryan's going to go through a few looks before this whole thing is over.
在这一切结束之前，瑞安还会尝试好几种造型。

595
00:29:58.510 --> 00:30:03.330
Well, Ryan in the scene, though, really puts Michael in his place.
不过，瑞安在那场戏里确实让迈克尔认清了自己的位置。

596
00:30:03.330 --> 00:30:05.090
And everyone, he's like, hey, you know what?
他对所有人说，嘿，你们知道吗？

597
00:30:05.250 --> 00:30:05.510
Enough.
