00:59:25.220 --> 00:59:27.420
And I love the scene.
我特别喜欢那个场景。

1211
00:59:28.320 --> 00:59:33.460
He goes on this very, very long, meandering story.
他讲了一个非常、非常长且漫无边际的故事。

1212
00:59:34.160 --> 00:59:38.380
But the way he connects it all is so real and organic.
但他把这一切串联起来的方式显得如此真实自然。

1213
00:59:38.640 --> 00:59:40.600
And you guys, we have been there.
伙计们，我们都有过这种经历。

1214
00:59:40.820 --> 00:59:46.880
We have all been there at that, you know, family gathering where someone gets up to talk and you're like,
我们都经历过那种家庭聚会，有人站起来说话，你会心想：

1215
00:59:46.880 --> 00:59:49.540
what, what are we, what are we talking about?
什么？我们到底在聊什么？

1216
00:59:50.220 --> 00:59:54.820
Yeah, you ask some innocent question like, oh my gosh, where'd you get your sweater?
没错，你问了一个无心的问题，比如“天哪，你的毛衣是在哪儿买的？”

1217
00:59:55.080 --> 01:00:00.840
And they're like, well, it was three years ago and it was raining that day.
然后他们就会说：“嗯，那是三年前的事了，那天还在下雨。”

1218
01:00:00.840 --> 01:00:01.560
I remember.
我记得。

1219
01:00:01.780 --> 01:00:06.660
I remember because I just got my hair done and they gave me a plastic net to put over it.
我记得是因为我刚做完头发，他们给了我一个塑料网套在头上。

1220
01:00:06.660 --> 01:00:13.800
Yes, and my friend Cynthia called and she said, well, you know, Cynthia, she had lived abroad.
对，然后我朋友辛西娅打来电话，她说——你知道辛西娅，她曾在国外住过。

1221
01:00:14.000 --> 01:00:17.400
And when she came back, she divorced and married that younger guy.
她回来后就离婚了，嫁给了那个年轻的小伙子。

1222
01:00:18.500 --> 01:00:19.900
Well, she did.
没错，她是嫁了。

1223
01:00:20.060 --> 01:00:26.840
But first, remember, she had that period of time where she went on that sex sabbatical.
但首先要记得，她还有过一段“性休假”的时期。

1224
01:00:27.020 --> 01:00:27.580
She did.
确实有过。

1225
01:00:27.760 --> 01:00:29.740
That's right about when she got that mole removed.
那差不多就是她去点掉那颗痣的时候。

1226
01:00:29.880 --> 01:00:31.500
Do you remember her dermatologist?
你还记得她的皮肤科医生吗？

1227
01:00:31.500 --> 01:00:33.460
He was such a nice guy.
他人真好。

1228
01:00:34.200 --> 01:00:35.240
Tall guy.
个子很高。

1229
01:00:35.480 --> 01:00:36.240
Tall guy.
个子很高。

1230
01:00:36.600 --> 01:00:36.860
Tall.
很高。

1231
01:00:37.680 --> 01:00:39.080
And had an accent.
而且有口音。

1232
01:00:39.980 --> 01:00:40.500
Yeah.
是啊。

1233
01:00:40.760 --> 01:00:42.740
But I could never figure out where he was from.
但我一直没听出来他是哪儿人。

1234
01:00:43.580 --> 01:00:44.100
Yeah.
是啊。

1235
01:00:44.400 --> 01:00:45.900
He made a very good dip.
他做的蘸酱特别好吃。

1236
01:00:46.720 --> 01:00:47.940
And you're like, what?
然后你就会想：什么？

1237
01:00:48.320 --> 01:00:50.360
You're like, where's the sweater from?
你心想：毛衣到底在哪儿买的？

1238
01:00:50.560 --> 01:00:51.440
Where's the sweater?
毛衣呢？

1239
01:00:51.680 --> 01:00:52.380
What did we just do?
我们刚才到底干了什么？

1240
01:00:52.500 --> 01:00:57.260
Jenna and I just completely improvised this random conversation.
珍娜和我刚才完全即兴编了这段乱七八糟的对话。

1241
01:00:57.260 --> 01:00:59.780
But you guys know you've been in this moment.
但你们都知道，你们肯定也经历过这种时刻。

1242
01:00:59.780 --> 01:01:03.180
Yeah, that was Robert Dunder.
对，那是罗伯特·邓德。

1243
01:01:03.360 --> 01:01:05.160
And so Michael throws him out.
所以迈克尔把他赶了出去。

1244
01:01:05.360 --> 01:01:08.000
Wait, can we also, sorry, this is hopping around.
等等，我们能不能也——抱歉，话题跳得有点远。

1245
01:01:08.200 --> 01:01:11.680
Can we also talk about how Michael introduces Robert to everyone?
我们能不能聊聊迈克尔是怎么把罗伯特介绍给所有人的？

1246
01:01:12.220 --> 01:01:12.740
Please.
请务必聊聊。

1247
01:01:13.040 --> 01:01:16.300
He says, who is this worthless bag of bones?
他说：“这个没用的老骨头是谁？”

1248
01:01:17.660 --> 01:01:22.220
That's his introduction to the founder of the company.
这就是他对公司创始人的介绍。

1249
01:01:22.220 --> 01:01:29.840
Well, we also had a fan question query from Erin Kearney, who says,
另外，我们收到了艾琳·卡尼的一个粉丝提问，她说：

1250
01:01:30.320 --> 01:01:38.420
Robert Dunder mentions Robert Mifflin's wife and her husband, Jerry Truppiano, a South Jersey guy who was tall.
罗伯特·邓德提到了罗伯特·米夫林的妻子和她的丈夫杰瑞·特鲁皮亚诺，一个来自南泽西、个子很高的人。

1251
01:01:38.420 --> 01:01:46.600
My question is, was this a reference to Jerry Truppiano, the longtime Red Sox broadcaster?
我的问题是，这是否是指长期担任红袜队播音员的杰瑞·特鲁皮亚诺？

1252
01:01:46.840 --> 01:01:53.740
I thought it might be because so many of the cast members and writers were Boston area folks.
我以为可能是，因为很多演员和编剧都是波士顿地区的人。

1253
01:01:53.740 --> 01:02:00.160
Well, I believe it to be true because Mike Schur, who wrote this episode, is a huge baseball fan.
嗯，我相信是真的，因为写这一集的迈克·舒尔是个超级棒球迷。

1254
01:02:00.680 --> 01:02:01.160
Yeah.
没错。

1255
01:02:01.320 --> 01:02:04.000
And I 100% think that's true.
而且我百分之百认为那是真的。

1256
01:02:04.240 --> 01:02:05.840
I think that's a good catch.
我觉得你观察得很仔细。

1257
01:02:06.300 --> 01:02:06.540
Yeah.
没错。

1258
01:02:08.490 --> 01:02:09.330
Good catch.
观察得真仔细。

1259
01:02:09.510 --> 01:02:11.890
Yeah, he snuck in a baseball player in there.
是啊，他偷偷塞进了一个棒球运动员的名字。

1260
01:02:13.450 --> 01:02:19.330
Well, as everyone is leaving the conference room, Ryan tells Michael, this day was a wash.
嗯，当大家离开会议室时，瑞安告诉迈克，这一天算是白忙活了。

1261
01:02:19.550 --> 01:02:23.550
Michael needs to embrace the new technology as the way of the future.
迈克需要拥抱新技术，将其视为未来的发展方向。

1262
01:02:24.330 --> 01:02:27.570
He really needs to get behind this new way of doing things.
他真的需要支持这种新的做事方式。

1263
01:02:28.370 --> 01:02:30.690
And Michael's like, no, you know what?
而迈克却说，不，你知道吗？

1264
01:02:30.830 --> 01:02:33.890
I'm going to prove you wrong that the old way is the best way.
我要向你证明你是错的，老方法才是最好的方法。

1265
01:02:34.070 --> 01:02:34.910
I'm going to prove you wrong.
我要证明你是错的。

1266
01:02:35.050 --> 01:02:36.210
We don't know what that's going to be.
我们不知道那会是什么。

1267
01:02:36.350 --> 01:02:37.810
But Michael says that.
但迈克确实这么说了。

1268
01:02:38.110 --> 01:02:40.070
And Jenna, there is a deleted scene.
还有珍娜，有一个删减片段。

1269
01:02:40.070 --> 01:02:40.850
I have to tell you,
我必须告诉你，

1270
01:02:41.010 --> 01:02:54.670
there's another department that's very stressed out about this because Ryan has a moment with the accountants where he shows them the new program they're going to use online for all of the accounting of Dunder Mifflin.
还有另一个部门对此感到非常焦虑，因为瑞安和会计们有个互动，他向他们展示了邓德·米夫林公司即将在线上使用的会计新程序。

1271
01:02:55.090 --> 01:02:57.650
And it's basically going to make them obsolete.
这基本上会让他们的工作变得多余。

1272
01:02:59.030 --> 01:02:59.290
Wow.
哇。

1273
01:03:01.070 --> 01:03:07.690
So people are freaking out about this, this new technology that Dunder Mifflin is going to be using.
所以大家对邓德·米夫林即将采用的这项新技术感到非常恐慌。

1274
01:03:08.410 --> 01:03:13.490
Well, we're going to get more of Michael's reaction to all of this in the next episode.
嗯，在下一集中，我们将看到迈克对这一切的更多反应。

1275
01:03:14.630 --> 01:03:20.450
We end this episode, though, with Angela and Dwight's dinner date.
不过，这一集的结尾是安吉拉和德怀特的晚餐约会。

1276
01:03:21.130 --> 01:03:21.650
Yes.
没错。

1277
01:03:22.010 --> 01:03:24.490
Well, lady, I have some location trivia.
好吧，女士，我有一些关于拍摄地的小知识。

1278
01:03:24.790 --> 01:03:26.930
I know you love a good location story.
我知道你喜欢听拍摄地的故事。

1279
01:03:27.350 --> 01:03:28.250
I do.
我确实喜欢。

1280
01:03:28.250 --> 01:03:36.130
And I will tell you, Ivy Burke will be very excited to hear what you have to say because Ivy would like to know where you filmed the Dwight and Angela dinner.
我得告诉你，艾薇·伯克听到你要说的内容一定会很兴奋，因为艾薇想知道你们是在哪里拍摄德怀特和安吉拉的晚餐戏份的。

1281
01:03:36.130 --> 01:03:39.890
We filmed it in the most beautiful neighborhood.
我们在一个非常美丽的社区拍摄的。

1282
01:03:40.310 --> 01:03:42.810
It's called the Malibu Lake Mountain Club.
它叫马里布湖山俱乐部。

1283
01:03:43.450 --> 01:03:49.670
It's a private community, so much so that there are no signs off the freeway for it.
那是一个私人社区，甚至连高速公路上都没有通往那里的指示牌。

1284
01:03:50.330 --> 01:03:50.830
Wow.
哇。

1285
01:03:50.830 --> 01:03:52.690
Yeah, it's like they don't want to be found.
是啊，就好像他们不想被人找到一样。

1286
01:03:52.930 --> 01:03:54.510
It's really, really beautiful.
那里真的非常非常漂亮。

1287
01:03:54.870 --> 01:03:57.530
This neighborhood was created in 1924.
这个社区建于1924年。

1288
01:03:57.910 --> 01:03:59.790
It was just like a valley.
当时那里就像个山谷。

1289
01:04:00.270 --> 01:04:03.350
And they made a lake, a man-made lake.
他们造了一个湖，一个人工湖。

1290
01:04:03.590 --> 01:04:06.210
And the members really wanted to keep it a secret.
成员们真的很想保守这个秘密。

1291
01:04:06.530 --> 01:04:11.610
So they removed the highway signs that gave directions to the lake, hoping to hide it from tourists.
所以他们拆除了高速公路上指向该湖的指示牌，希望能避开游客。

1292
01:04:11.610 --> 01:04:17.170
In 1936, they built a clubhouse with a ballroom and a large patio.
1936年，他们建造了一个带舞厅和大露台的会所。

1293
01:04:17.250 --> 01:04:22.530
And it had a speakeasy poker room and a mural of the original members.
里面还有一个地下酒吧风格的扑克室和一幅原始成员的壁画。

1294
01:04:22.630 --> 01:04:26.510
And only members can use the lake and the swimming pool and the tennis court.
只有会员才能使用湖泊、游泳池和网球场。

1295
01:04:26.690 --> 01:04:28.210
So it's this little private community.
所以这是一个小小的私人社区。

1296
01:04:28.810 --> 01:04:31.810
Ronald Reagan was the honorary mayor.
罗纳德·里根曾是那里的名誉市长。

1297
01:04:32.150 --> 01:04:35.730
And technically, that's the first political office he ever held.
从技术上讲，那是他担任的第一个政治职务。

1298
01:04:36.330 --> 01:04:36.830
Wow.
哇。

1299
01:04:37.230 --> 01:04:37.690
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1300
01:04:38.370 --> 01:04:40.310
Now, let me ask you a question.
现在，让我问你一个问题。

1301
01:04:41.530 --> 01:04:48.550
Did you film at this location because this lake is going to feature prominently in the next episode?
你们在这里取景，是因为这个湖会在下一集里有重要戏份吗？

1302
01:04:49.090 --> 01:04:49.950
Ding, ding, ding, ding, ding.
答对了，答对了，答对了。

1303
01:04:50.190 --> 01:04:53.630
Okay, so we had this location for one day.
好吧，我们在这个场地只有一天的拍摄时间。

1304
01:04:54.150 --> 01:04:58.990
Dwight and Angela filmed their dinner date in the lodge at Malibu Lake, their restaurant.
德怀特和安吉拉在马里布湖的旅馆里拍摄了他们的晚餐约会，也就是他们的餐厅。

1305
01:04:59.270 --> 01:05:04.610
And then we will see what happens to Michael and Dwight with the lake in the next episode.
然后我们会在下一集里看到迈克尔和德怀特在湖边发生了什么。

1306
01:05:04.770 --> 01:05:06.590
But that was all the same day.
但那都是在同一天拍的。

1307
01:05:06.590 --> 01:05:08.450
We filmed our scene at night.
我们是在晚上拍的那场戏。

1308
01:05:08.650 --> 01:05:10.510
So, Jenna, I had a late call time.
所以，珍娜，我的通告时间很晚。

1309
01:05:10.690 --> 01:05:11.050
Oh.
哦。

1310
01:05:11.430 --> 01:05:13.090
There was this huge moon.
当时月亮特别大。

1311
01:05:13.090 --> 01:05:19.230
And after we did the scene, I walked out on this floating dock and just watched the moon for a minute.
拍完那场戏后，我走到浮动码头上，盯着月亮看了一会儿。

1312
01:05:19.470 --> 01:05:22.870
And it was just like, you know, one of those magical nights on set where you're like,
那种感觉，你知道，就像片场里那些神奇的夜晚，你会觉得，

1313
01:05:22.990 --> 01:05:26.390
this feels so cool because it's really a beautiful little area.
这感觉太棒了，因为这确实是一个非常美丽的小地方。

1314
01:05:26.770 --> 01:05:30.070
And Steve Carell has made their official website.
史蒂夫·卡瑞尔还上了他们的官网。

1315
01:05:30.270 --> 01:05:30.970
Ready for this?
准备好听这个了吗？

1316
01:05:30.970 --> 01:05:35.470
It says, just a few of the famous faces that have shot here.
上面写着，这里拍摄过的一些名人面孔。

1317
01:05:35.730 --> 01:05:38.090
Charlie Chaplin, W.C.
查理·卓别林，W.C.

1318
01:05:38.230 --> 01:05:42.430
Fields, Diane Lane, Lloyd Bridges, Lucille Ball, Steve Carell,
菲尔兹，黛安·莲恩，劳埃德·布里奇斯，露西尔·鲍尔，史蒂夫·卡瑞尔，

1319
01:05:42.950 --> 01:05:44.690
Betty Davis, Henry Fonda.
贝蒂·戴维斯，亨利·方达。

1320
01:05:44.690 --> 01:05:45.770
It goes on and on.
名单长着呢。

1321
01:05:45.930 --> 01:05:47.550
But Steve Carell made the liSt.
但史蒂夫·卡瑞尔居然上了名单。

1322
01:05:47.890 --> 01:05:49.030
I love that.
我喜欢这个。

1323
01:05:49.550 --> 01:05:50.630
I know, right?
是吧？

1324
01:05:50.790 --> 01:05:51.390
Really fun.
真有意思。

1325
01:05:51.390 --> 01:05:55.710
But this scene between Rain and I, I just loved doing it.
但我跟雷恩的那场戏，我特别喜欢演。

1326
01:05:55.950 --> 01:06:01.430
We took the scene apart because Dwight is hoping that it's one thing.
我们拆解了那场戏，因为德怀特希望那是另一回事。

1327
01:06:01.970 --> 01:06:04.690
Angela's trying for it to be a reconciliation.
安吉拉则试图让它成为一次和解。

1328
01:06:04.690 --> 01:06:06.950
And then she just can't do it.
但最后她还是做不到。

1329
01:06:07.610 --> 01:06:11.330
And they wanted me to be able to show that emotion in my face that I was trying.
他们希望我能通过面部表情表现出那种我在努力尝试的情绪。

1330
01:06:11.970 --> 01:06:13.730
And then I just couldn't get past it.
然后我就是过不去心里那道坎。

1331
01:06:13.910 --> 01:06:14.850
I couldn't get past it.
我过不去。

1332
01:06:15.010 --> 01:06:18.910
And it's got a couplet of dialogue that I love.
里面有两句我很喜欢的对白。

1333
01:06:19.290 --> 01:06:22.270
It's when Angela says, I heard a joke today.
就是安吉拉说，我今天听了个笑话。

1334
01:06:22.690 --> 01:06:25.390
And Dwight says, oh, that's funny.
德怀特说，哦，那挺好笑的。

1335
01:06:25.630 --> 01:06:28.670
And Angela says, yes, it was.
安吉拉说，是的，确实好笑。

1336
01:06:30.720 --> 01:06:31.220
Yeah.
是啊。

1337
01:06:33.610 --> 01:06:36.130
Well, this scene is just beautiful.
嗯，这场戏真的很美。

1338
01:06:36.130 --> 01:06:38.990
It's beautiful for all the reasons you said.
正如你所说，它美在方方面面。

1339
01:06:39.230 --> 01:06:46.930
It's funny, but then it breaks your heart because your performance, Angela, we really see your
它很有趣，但又让人心碎，因为你的表演，安吉拉，我们真的看到了你的

1340
01:06:46.930 --> 01:06:49.150
character's heart breaking in this moment.
角色在这一刻心碎了。

1341
01:06:49.370 --> 01:06:51.370
And it's just real.
而且非常真实。

1342
01:06:51.590 --> 01:06:53.490
Like you aren't playing it for comedy.
你不是为了搞笑而演。

1343
01:06:53.490 --> 01:06:54.670
It's just real.
它就是真实的。

1344
01:06:55.190 --> 01:07:01.090
And these are the moments of The Office that I'm so proud of as a television comedy that
这些时刻让我为《办公室》这部电视喜剧感到无比自豪，

1345
01:07:01.090 --> 01:07:03.730
we took these moments to get really real.
我们抓住了这些时刻，让它变得非常真实。

1346
01:07:05.090 --> 01:07:06.030
Thanks, ladies.
谢谢你们，女士们。

1347
01:07:06.130 --> 01:07:06.690
Thanks.
谢谢。

1348
01:07:06.910 --> 01:07:08.410
I really enjoyed the storyline.
我真的很喜欢这个故事线。

1349
01:07:08.830 --> 01:07:11.770
I love Dwight and Angela being together.
我喜欢德怀特和安吉拉在一起。

1350
01:07:11.970 --> 01:07:14.570
And I loved when they were at odds.
我也喜欢他们针锋相对的时候。

1351
01:07:14.750 --> 01:07:16.370
It was equally fun to play.
演起来也同样有趣。

1352
01:07:17.030 --> 01:07:17.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1353
01:07:17.570 --> 01:07:18.810
It's such a good dynamic.
这种互动太棒了。

1354
01:07:19.210 --> 01:07:23.390
